WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.063
(upbeat music)

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:08.243
^- Hello, I'm here with Bobby.

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:09.483
^- Hi.

00:00:09.483 --> 00:00:10.720
- [Ella] Bobby was one of the first

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:13.013
BuzzFeed Video employees back in the day.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.303
When did you start?

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:15.350
- [Bobby] Like 2013.

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:18.400
- [Ella] Back in an office that we called Stony Bros.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.490
- And this is the backdrop of early days

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:23.490
where it's like, what is a BuzzFeed video?

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.410
- Yeah, so it didn't help our image at all.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:29.870
Like, a few times, we had celebrities come by,

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.263
and I was like, yep, this is our trash hole.

00:00:33.392 --> 00:00:34.225
- [Bobby] Yeah.

00:00:34.225 --> 00:00:35.058
- We didn't have interns

00:00:35.058 --> 00:00:37.300
or really anyone to help out with anything,

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.036
so I remember that dishes would pile up in the sink.

00:00:40.036 --> 00:00:40.869
- [Bobby] Mm-hmm.

00:00:40.869 --> 00:00:41.862
There was a huge gnat--

00:00:41.862 --> 00:00:42.695
- There was a gnat problem.

00:00:42.695 --> 00:00:44.900
- I think we ended up moving because of the gnats,

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:46.260
'cause we just didn't want to deal with it anymore.

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:47.960
- We were just like, here, just take it, gnats.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.860
- There were so many, and I remember in the videos,

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:53.693
you could sometimes see them flying through the frame.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:56.160
- Guys, I found out why we have fruit flies.

00:00:56.299 --> 00:00:59.500
(singing dramatically)

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.960
- Then after that, we moved to a house.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.630
- My office was in a bedroom,

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:06.280
and other people working at Buzzfeed

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:07.963
would just lay on the bed.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.860
- I had my one bed that I would work from,

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.372
and I would be all cozy, and I would be editing from it.

00:01:13.372 --> 00:01:14.205
- Yeah.

00:01:14.205 --> 00:01:15.890
- What were the things that you did,

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:16.900
like, your favorite things

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.317
that you did while you were at Buzzfeed?

00:01:18.317 --> 00:01:19.443
- The Creep videos.

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:23.010
^- Yeah, they were a hugely popular series

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:25.430
^back in the day, starring Andrew Ilnyckyj.

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:27.013
How did that come about?

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:31.210
That was such a funny, very unique video series.

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:32.464
- [Bobby] So, Andrew was an intern at the time.

00:01:32.464 --> 00:01:33.297
- [Ella] Yeah.

00:01:33.297 --> 00:01:34.550
- [Bobby] And I just liked his voice.

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:36.210
If he says anything, it's hilarious.

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:38.300
And we did this video, I think it's called

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.550
Tea Versus Coffee?

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:40.500
- Yes!
- Where it's just

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.733
his voiceover, and it was so funny,

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:45.520
and we were trying to figure out something,

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:47.260
and I don't know how it came up,

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:48.983
but the Creep thing came up.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.400
There was a mystery about him.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.163
^- Yeah, his voice was really deep.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:55.343
- I really like your style.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:58.840
I think I'll follow you.

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:00.790
- The first one you shot was in Stony Bros.

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:03.330
^- It was just like the creepy person in the office,

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:05.240
^and so, there was no frame,

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:06.640
and it was just him being a weirdo,

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.410
and that's maybe my favorite one

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:09.700
because there is no point to it.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:11.650
- There's no point, and it's just like,

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:13.810
back in the day, we didn't really have any lights.

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:16.303
The vibe of this video is very shadowy,

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.535
and it's like, what is happening?

00:02:18.535 --> 00:02:22.433
- What was the one that catapulted into super stardom?

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:23.450
- [Ella] 'Cause that one didn't really take off.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:26.390
^- [Bobby] No, I think it was Creepy Things Girls Do?

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:29.030
^- [Ella] Yeah, that had like five million views.

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:29.863
- [Bobby] Yeah.

00:02:29.863 --> 00:02:32.003
It was like our biggest hit of all time, at the time.

00:02:32.458 --> 00:02:34.623
- [Andrew] I'm not wearing any underwear.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:36.650
- I knew we hit the big time when some

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:39.187
German magazine called, Buzzfeed, and was like,

00:02:39.187 --> 00:02:41.387
"We want to interview Andrew," or something.

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:42.440
And I was like, what?

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:44.640
- Yeah, and it was just this thing where

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.710
he didn't even have a name, really.

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:47.543
- [Bobby] No.

00:02:47.543 --> 00:02:48.740
He was just called "Buzzfeed Creep."

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:49.620
- And, to be fair,

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:53.570
I don't think Andrew completely loved being the creep.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:54.934
Like, he was resistant.

00:02:54.934 --> 00:02:55.767
- [Ella] He did it.

00:02:55.767 --> 00:02:57.720
- [Bobby] And the other thing that I enjoyed

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:59.940
about the Creep series was my friend Matt,

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:03.080
who I knew since film school, basically was

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:05.670
the punching bag in every Creep.

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:08.343
So, I just enjoyed taunting Matt.

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:09.540
- [Matt] I just have no idea why they

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:10.713
have to make three Hobbit movies.

00:03:10.713 --> 00:03:12.230
(glass smashing)

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:14.610
- He was a great character in all of it.

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:16.210
Our favorite role, that we always

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:18.230
talk about, when he played Gerald.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.580
- [Bobby] That was a roommate video.

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:20.413
- [Ella] Yeah.

00:03:20.413 --> 00:03:22.210
- [Bobby] That was my last video at Buzzfeed,

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:24.340
was the roommate video, and I,

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:26.173
of course, had to torture Matt.

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:27.790
I don't know where the hell it came from.

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:31.093
But it was this weird character who had a dead squirrel,

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:32.240
that he needed to refrigerate.

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:33.820
- We reference Gerald all the time.

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:37.143
So, Bobby, what have you been up to all these years?

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.360
- [Bobby] I made a feature film.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:39.300
- [Ella] Oh, my god!

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.450
- [Bobby] It's called, The Cleanse.

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:41.283
- [Ella] When is it out?

00:03:41.283 --> 00:03:42.330
- It comes out May 4th.

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:43.500
- Oh my gosh, you guys.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:44.950
If you guys want to check out the trailer,

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:46.923
the link is in the description below.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:47.793
Give it a watch.

00:03:47.793 --> 00:03:48.720
Give it a thumbs up.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:52.060
Thank you Bobby, for coming, for reminiscing.

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:53.870
Hopefully you guys will check out his movie,

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:55.364
and hopefully we'll see you back here.

00:03:55.364 --> 00:03:56.393
- Well, thank you.

00:03:56.398 --> 00:03:57.349
- Goodbye, little guy.

00:03:57.349 --> 00:03:58.182
- Bye.

00:03:58.182 --> 00:03:59.015
- Bye.

00:03:59.582 --> 00:04:03.082
(retro electronic music)

